; Source: HSPICE User Guide: Basic Simulation and Analysis, H-2013.03,
; chapter 10 "Sources and Stimuli", "Specifying a Digital Vector File and
; Mixed Mode Stimuli", "Digital Vector File Example" (its statements; the
; manual's comments are summarized here). The manual states: the signal
; names are v1, va[0], va[1], vb1 ... vb12 (the innermost [] is the range,
; MSB:LSB); vb12-vb5 are outputs when v1 is high and vb4-vb1 when it is low;
; every signal has a 1 ns delay, va 1.5 ns; rise and fall times 1.2 ns; VIH
; 3.3 V for v1 and 5.0 V for vb; va and vb switch at VTH 1.75 V.
radix 1 2 444
vname v1 va[[1:0]] vb[12:1]
io i o bbb
tunit ns
enable v1 0 0 FF0
enable ~v1 0 0 00F
tdelay 1.0
tdelay 1.5 0 3 000
slope 1.2
vih 3.3 1 0 000
vih 5.0 0 0 FFF
vth 1.75 0 1 FFF
10.0 1 3 FFF
20.0 0 2 AFF
30.0 1 0 888
